# Droplet-first CrewAI / Langfuse

Production crew runs, secrets, and Langfuse tracing belong on the **parkinglot Droplet** (`/opt/workspaces/parkinglot`), not the Mac clone (`main · local`).

## Source of truth

| What | Where |
|------|--------|
| All production secrets | `deploy/.env` on Droplet |
| Crew overrides (Langfuse, OpenAI) | `services/crew/.env` on Droplet — synced from `deploy/.env` |
| Langfuse API host (US, hardwired) | `config/langfuse.yaml` → `https://us.cloud.langfuse.com` |
| Crew runs | SSH / Cursor Remote → Droplet |

## On Droplet (do this)

```bash
cd /opt/workspaces/parkinglot
./scripts/droplet-crew-install.sh          # once
./scripts/droplet-crew-env-sync.sh         # after deploy/.env changes
./scripts/droplet-crew-langfuse-setup.sh   # paste LANGFUSE keys only (US host is automatic)
./scripts/droplet-crew-audit.sh            # tools preflight
./scripts/droplet-crew-smoke.sh            # Langfuse check + preflight
./scripts/droplet-crew-cron-install.sh     # weekly Mon 06:00 UTC cron (once)
.venv/bin/parking-crew audit               # full LLM audit when OPENAI_API_KEY set
```

## Avoid on Mac clone

- Do **not** store production `DATABASE_URL`, Slack tokens, or Langfuse secrets in Mac `services/crew/.env` unless explicitly mirroring for offline dev (`sync-crew-secrets.sh --pull-from-droplet`).
- Do **not** default crew DB to `127.0.0.1` on Droplet — use managed Postgres from `deploy/.env`.
- Do **not** set `LANGFUSE_HOST` to EU `cloud.langfuse.com` — US URL is hardwired in `config/langfuse.yaml`.

## Mac-only actions

- `make droplet-sync` — push code to Droplet
- `./scripts/run-crew-tests.sh` — CI-style unit tests (no production secrets)
- Open workspace via `parkinglot-droplet.code-workspace` for agent work on the server
